sect.p:
Act of 1988 means
               the Data
                  Protection Act 1988;

authorised
               officer means a person appointed, or deemed to be appointed, to be an
               authorised officer under section 129;

Commissioner has
               the meaning assigned to it by section 15 and includes a member of staff
               authorised to act in place of a Commissioner under section 18;

local authority
               means a local authority within the meaning of section 2 of the Local
                  Government Act 2001;

political party
               means a political party registered in the Register of Political Parties in accordance
               with section 25 of the Electoral Act 1992;

(b) a subsidiary (within the
               meaning of section 7 of the Act of 2014) of a company referred to in paragraph
                  (a);

(b)
               section 2(7) and
               (8);

(d)
               section
               5(1)(d);

(f)
               section 11(3) and
               (4)(b);
